.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-auth-logout - Remove the key from this profile and revoke it on the server


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro auth logout [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Keys created by 'gyro auth login' are revoked on the server and removed from the profile.
A key you pasted with 'gyro configure' is only removed locally (it may be used elsewhere); add --revoke to revoke it too.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for logout

.PP
\fB--keep-key\fP[=false]
	only remove the key locally, never revoke it

.PP
\fB--revoke\fP[=false]
	also revoke a key that was not created by gyro auth login


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
